=== HYPOTHESIS ===
# p_b4f2 — Standard split, glasses at coffee table, mug at sink (fork of p_4c7d)

Forked from p_4c7d to fix the glasses and the mug. The parent's glasses_priya ON_PERSON block (7:00–22:00) failed on 3 sightings (0.13 hit rate): the glasses are actually at the coffee table in the afternoon and evening, and at the nightstand at 18:00 and 23:00. I replace the ON_PERSON block with two coffee_table blocks (14:00–17:00 and 19:50–22:30) and keep the nightstand as the base. The parent placed mug_elena's resting spot at cupboard_k1, but the 03:00 passes consistently show it at sink_k1 (×3 on weekdays), and the 22:00 pass also shows sink_k1. I move the base to sink_k1. I also add the remote at coffee_table 13:00–16:00 (sightings at 14:00 and 15:00) and tighten the dog food bag evening window to 19:50–21:00 (the 19:00 pass still catches it at the pantry). The dinner window stays at 19:50–21:00 as in the parent, but I add a separate glass/water-bottle window at 19:00–21:00 since glass_priya is at the table by 19:00 while plate_elena is not until 20:00.

What sets this apart from p_4c7d: no ON_PERSON glasses, mug_elena at sink_k1, remote at coffee table in the afternoon, and a split dinner setup (glasses at 19, plates at 20). What would refute it: glasses_priya sighted ON_PERSON at 16:00, or mug_elena at the cupboard at 03:00 on a weekday.

